A $2 \times 2$ factorial on DocRED (count $\in \{16, 32\}$, BCS median split at 0.55; $n = 70$) yields a larger interaction estimate (+5.7\,pp, 95\% CI [$-$1.6, 13.0]): the BCS effect is $-$10.6\,pp at count 16 but only $-$4.9\,pp at count 32. TOST at $\pm 3$\,pp is not established ($p = 0.77$). The asymmetry likely reflects baseline compression: at count 32, accuracy approaches chance ($\sim$49\%), leaving less room for confusability to further reduce performance. We therefore restrict the bounded-interaction conclusion to sentence-level RE.

